WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.150
Steven Ogg, the guy who plays Negan's brutal
right-hand man Simon on The Walking Dead,

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.580
is a classic "that guy."

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.190
You know you've seen him in… something…
somewhere… but you can't just quite put

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.060
your finger on it.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.920
So where exactly have you seen that beautiful
mustache before?

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.820
Here's why Simon from The Walking Dead looks
so familiar.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.420
Mail Order Bride

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:26.839
Ogg's official screen debut came in a cameo
in the 1999 romcom flop Giving It Up, and

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:31.149
he followed that with a guest appearance on
an episode of Law &amp; Order in 2000.

00:00:31.149 --> 00:00:36.960
But his first major role came in the 2003
mob comedy Mail Order bride, which featured

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.730
Danny Aiello and Sopranos alum Vincent Pastore
alongside Ogg in a movie The New York Times

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.240
called "a strained, incoherent farce."

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.520
"Find the broad."

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.300
"Broad?"

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.500
"Yeah… a broad."

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.800
"A… a broad?"

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.940
Hey, everyone has to start somewhere.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.360
Grand Theft Auto V

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:04.020
After more than a decade toiling away in bit
roles and bad films like Mail Order Bride,

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.660
Ogg finally got his big break in 2013 by switching
mediums.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.730
He wound up being cast to do voicework and
motion capture for the hit video game Grand

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:18.400
Theft Auto V. Ogg played the fan-favorite,
bank-robbing meth-chef Trevor Philips, one

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.590
of the game's three main characters.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:24.420
And he was pretty gratified that fans seemed
to love the result of his work.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:29.340
He told Buzzfeed, "I have been so thrilled
that the GTA fans have responded so positively

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.520
to the performance.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.750
They have enjoyed his impulsive, psychopathic
nature but have reveled in his humor."

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:35.920
"Hey there, Wade."

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.020
"Did you meet Debra?"

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.790
"Ooh, interesting lady."

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.540
"I should probably go say, 'Hi.'"

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.260
"I wouldn't…"

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.620
Seems that Ogg doesn't keep his unique brand
of insanity restricted to video games, though.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.939
"I wanna do something else, move on to the
next thing.

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:51.950
Probably zombies."

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.800
Unforgettable

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.700
CBS cop drama Unforgettable, which followed
the daily exploits of a detective with photographic

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.710
memory, managed to get canceled three times
— but not before Ogg popped up as sleazy

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.890
receptionist Larry Yablonski in the episode
"Day of the Jackie."

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:12.891
Wearing an open shirt over a string vest and
sporting a wild mess of greasy hair, this

00:02:12.891 --> 00:02:17.260
is the first time the Canadian character actor
showcased the kind of unkempt crazy that Walking

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.920
Dead fans would later love to hate.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.820
Person of Interest

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.940
Ogg made another cameo on a CBS procedural
when he popped up as an angry barfly in a

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.710
season three episode of Person of Interest.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:32.990
Luckily for Ogg's character, the authorities
happen to already be in the bar because the

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:37.560
sailor he's fighting has been tagged as a
potential victim of an upcoming crime, so

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.170
Ogg managed to get off without too bad a beatdown.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.340
​Broad City

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:46.350
Ogg made a memorable guest appearance in Comedy
Central's Broad City in 2014.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:51.350
After stars Ilana Glazer and Abbi Jacobson
manage to get locked out of their apartment,

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.630
they call for a locksmith and receive a lot
more than they bargained for when Ogg shows

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.660
up.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.690
"Yolanda"

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.760
"Mmm, Yolanda.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.350
So where is it you sleep?"

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.350
"What?"

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.780
"Which apartment's yours?"

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.400
Even though the guest appearance lasted just
a couple minutes, Ogg told The Calgary Herald

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.840
that he still gets recognized at airports
for the role of Creepy Locksmith.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.180
Murdoch Mysteries

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:20.900
Based on the series of novels by British-Canadian
author Maureen Jennings, Murdoch Mysteries

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:26.950
explores crime in 20th-century Ontario through
the eyes of detective William Murdoch.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:31.560
Ogg turned up on the show in Season 8 episode
"Glory Days," trimming down his handlebar

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.730
to a respectable shortness to play Bat Masterson,
a legendary frontier lawman who's tracked

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.560
infamous bandits Butch Cassidy and the Sundance
Kid to Toronto.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.840
Despite being a proud Canadian, Ogg played
Masterson as a brash American unimpressed

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.770
by law enforcement north of the border, something
he told Dorkshelf he played up on purpose

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:51.870
to prove a point.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.620
"So many people come up to me and say, 'There
is no difference between Canadians and Americans.'

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.300
Well, I disagree."

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.640
"Where are your guns?"

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.600
"We don't carry guns.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.160
North of the border, we rely on our wits."

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:04.760
"Ohh.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.840
Fat lot of good your wits just did us."

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:07.900
Better Call Saul

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.150
Another of AMC's shows that Ogg has worked
on, Better Call Saul has evolved from a Breaking

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.160
Bad spinoff into a show more than capable
of standing on its own two feet.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.700
Star Bob Odenkirk is the linchpin of the prequel's
success, but he's given ample help by the

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:27.300
show's supporting cast, in particular Jonathan
Banks, who plays ex-cop Mike.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.220
And in a memorable scene from season one,
Ogg got to be on the receiving end of a short

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.120
and painful life lesson from Mike.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.840
Man, that's a tough way to make a living.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.060
The Escort

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:45.279
Dark indie romance The Escort is the story
of two sex addicts brought together by a mutually

00:04:45.279 --> 00:04:50.710
beneficial arrangement — a down-and-out
journalist in need of a good story and a Stanford-educated

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:53.590
prostitute in need of protection from her
clients.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:54.380
One of those clients?

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.040
Yup.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:55.540
It's Ogg.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.240
This time around, the Oggster actually backs
down before getting punched, smacked, or beaten.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.580
Who says an old Ogg can't learn new tricks?

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.280
Westworld

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.560
We saw a lot of Steven Ogg in Westworld.

00:05:07.569 --> 00:05:12.379
Not a lot in terms of screen time, but a lot
of Ogg himself, as the actor shot scenes naked

00:05:12.379 --> 00:05:17.259
for HBO's hit sci-fi series about robotic
hosts programmed to entertain guests in an

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.700
Old West themed amusement park.

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:23.919
His character, Rebus, is one such host, a
villainous cowboy who plays a major part in

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.940
a narrative involving fellow host Dolores
Abernathy.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.640
Old Spice ads

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:35.020
In 2016 Ogg began portraying the so-called
King of Products Bob Giovanni in an advertising

00:05:35.029 --> 00:05:39.659
campaign for the "Hardest Working Collection"
range, a new series of deodorant from retro

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.260
men's groomer Old Spice.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.640
The company devised a tongue-in-cheek plan
to go back to the days when it offered a money-back

00:05:45.659 --> 00:05:51.909
guarantee if Old Spice wasn't up for the job,
resurrecting its 1-800-PROVE-IT hotline and

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:55.020
launching some hilariously bad parody ads
starring Ogg.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.080
"So men can focus on other, more important
things."

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.580
Thanks for watching!

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.340
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.060
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

